5. She grew up in a British household where drinking tea was a common family practice. (Verbatim: "I don't know if this is a British thing but I had to learn how to drink tea... everyone else in my family that was drinking tea")

6. As a child, she was responsible for making tea and coffee for visiting family members every Sunday. (Verbatim: "whenever my nan nana elia would come visit every single sunday and um and that's when i would be made to go make tea and coffee for everybody")

7. She once drank golden syrup straight as a child, treating it like a beverage. (Verbatim: "there's a short that covers my story about drinking golden syrup and just eating sugar")

8. She initially misunderstood espresso, thinking it was a small or children's version of coffee due to its size. (Verbatim: "I look back at the shot, and I'm like, oh no, I've ordered a coffee for babies... This must be for small children")

9. She once ordered a double espresso thinking it would be a larger, "full-sized" coffee, not understanding the meaning of the term. (Verbatim: "double espresso, nice, that's probably for a larger child, or maybe an adult, I shall get it, and finally get my full-sized coffee")

