1. She grew up in a household with different rules for boys and girls, experiencing gender-based double standards. (Verbatim: "some good old-fashioned misogyny where um where the rules were different because they were boys um to me who is who's girl")

2. She has two older brothers, referred to as the "ellie bros," who were given more freedom than she was as a child. (Verbatim: "both early bros were considered responsible enough to like be able to walk outside on their own um and i i was not")

3. As a child, she was forced to have short hair and often wore hand-me-down clothes, making her feel scruffy and unkept. (Verbatim: "i'd literally be the scruffiest looking child as well i'd be like this kid in like her heckin hand me downs with her with her little short hair that she was forced to have")

4. She didn’t care about appearance as a child because she felt there was no one to be presentable to. (Verbatim: "why do i have to look nice um and it wasn't until i was older when i figured out that um turns out people treat you differently they treat you differently based on how you look")

