6. Her mother ("mama elia") drinks coffee and does not like tea. (Verbatim: "mama elia has coffee she doesn't like tea")

7. Her father ("papa elia") takes his coffee with two teaspoons of sugar and some milk. (Verbatim: "papa elia has two two two teaspoons of sugar and some milk")

8. Her grandmother ("nana elia") prefers her tea milkier and uses sweeteners instead of sugar, which she brings herself. (Verbatim: "nana elia prefers hers on the milkier side and has sweeteners no no sugar she prefers she prefers sweeteners which she brings herself wherever she goes")

9. She discovered late in life that people are treated differently based on appearance, which she describes as an "awful lesson." (Verbatim: "i discovered that awful that awful lesson much later on like too too too too too too too late")

