4. She has difficulty pronouncing certain English sounds, particularly the "R", and is self-conscious about it. (Verbatim: "I have an issue with the way I pronounce them... I gotta hold back my R's.")  
5. She attempts to speak in Received Pronunciation (RP) to sound more formal or "fancy". (Verbatim: "I speak RP. I need to be able to speak RP.")  
